# Jobs & workers (v1)

## When to create a job
Create a job if:
- it involves external network calls
- it must survive restarts/deploys
- it can be retried safely
Examples:
- ActivityPub delivery
- ActivityPub inbox processing
- Monad indexing / reconciliation
- DM notification fanout

## Job execution model
- Use a Postgres jobs table.
- Workers claim jobs with locking (e.g. SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED).
- Jobs support:
  - attempts + maxAttempts
  - nextRunAt (backoff)
  - lastError
  - correlationId

## Reliability
- Prefer “write DB state + enqueue job” in the same transaction when correctness matters.
- Avoid in-process fire-and-forget for anything important.
